---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CalculatorCard from '../components/CalculatorCard.astro';
import { calculators, categories } from '../data/calculators.js';
import { absoluteSiteUrl } from '../data/site.js';

const description = 'Accurate, fast online calculators for finance, health, math, dates, education, and everyday life.';
const homeUrl = absoluteSiteUrl(import.meta.env.BASE_URL);
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    { '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'ClearCalc Tools', url: homeUrl, description },
    {
      '@type': 'ItemList',
      name: 'ClearCalc calculators',
      itemListElement: calculators.map((item, index) => ({
        '@type': 'ListItem',
        position: index + 1,
        name: item.title,
        url: absoluteSiteUrl(`/calculators/${item.slug}/`)
      }))
    }
  ]
};
const jsonLd = JSON.stringify(schema).replaceAll('<', '\\u003c');
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
---
<Layout title="Free Online Calculators | ClearCalc Tools" description={description}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={jsonLd} />
  <section class="hero"><div><span class="eyebrow">FREE • FAST • PRIVATE</span><h1>Calculate with confidence.</h1><p>Clear answers for money, health, school, and everyday decisions. No signup required.</p><a class="button" href="#calculators">Explore calculators</a></div><div class="hero-panel"><span>Quick calculation</span><strong>Simple inputs.</strong><strong>Clear results.</strong><strong>Useful explanations.</strong></div></section>
  <section class="trust"><span>✓ No account</span><span>✓ Mobile friendly</span><span>✓ Transparent formulas</span></section>
  <section id="calculators" class="section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">CALCULATOR LIBRARY</span><h2>Popular calculators</h2></div><p>Choose a tool and get an answer in seconds.</p></div>
    {categories.map((category) => {
      const categoryId = category.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').replace(/^-|-$/g, '');
      return <div class="category-section" id={categoryId}><h3 class="category-title">{category}</h3><div class="card-grid">{calculators.filter((item) => item.category === category).map((item) => <CalculatorCard item={item} />)}</div></div>;
    })}
  </section>
  <section class="content-band"><h2>Designed to make numbers easier</h2><p>Every ClearCalc tool focuses on one job, shows the formula it uses, and runs in your browser. Nothing you type is sent to a ClearCalc account. Results are estimates. For an important money or health decision, compare the result with a qualified professional and with the lender, school, or clinician who has your actual terms.</p><p>The <a href={`${base}calculators/mortgage-calculator/`}>mortgage payment calculator</a> and the <a href={`${base}calculators/loan-calculator/`}>loan payment calculator</a> both use standard monthly amortization, with taxes and fees left out so the interest math stays visible. The <a href={`${base}calculators/compound-interest-calculator/`}>compound interest calculator</a> projects a balance from a starting amount and end-of-month deposits. Health tools cover <a href={`${base}calculators/bmi-calculator/`}>adult BMI</a> from kilograms and centimeters and a <a href={`${base}calculators/calorie-calculator/`}>maintenance-calorie estimate</a> from the Mifflin–St Jeor equation for men or women. Everyday math includes a <a href={`${base}calculators/percentage-calculator/`}>percentage calculator</a>, a <a href={`${base}calculators/tip-calculator/`}>tip split</a>, a <a href={`${base}calculators/discount-calculator/`}>percent-off sale price</a>, and a <a href={`${base}calculators/length-converter/`}>length converter</a> from meters to feet, inches, yards, or kilometers. Date tools count an <a href={`${base}calculators/age-calculator/`}>exact age</a> or the <a href={`${base}calculators/date-difference-calculator/`}>days between two dates</a>. Work and pay includes a <a href={`${base}calculators/uk-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>2026/27 take-home pay calculator</a> for employees in England, Wales, and Northern Ireland. The <a href={`${base}calculators/gpa-calculator/`}>GPA calculator</a> averages four unweighted grades on a 4.0 scale, and the <a href={`${base}calculators/final-exam-grade-calculator/`}>final exam grade calculator</a> solves for the score a weighted final needs. Home projects include a <a href={`${base}calculators/concrete-slab-calculator/`}>concrete slab calculator</a> that turns feet and inches into bags and cubic yards.</p><p>Five later tools answer questions the earlier pages leave open. The <a href={`${base}calculators/new-york-paycheck-calculator/`}>2026 New York paycheck calculator</a> adds New York State tax and, when you ask for it, New York City resident tax. The <a href={`${base}calculators/alberta-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>Alberta take-home pay calculator</a> uses the 2026 Alberta brackets, CPP, and EI, with no provincial health premium. The <a href={`${base}calculators/nsw-stamp-duty-calculator/`}>NSW stamp duty calculator</a> applies 2026/27 New South Wales transfer duty, including the first home buyer concession. The <a href={`${base}calculators/uk-student-loan-repayment-calculator/`}>UK student loan repayment calculator</a> estimates a 2026/27 Plan 1, Plan 2, Plan 4, Plan 5, or postgraduate deduction, which the England take-home page does not subtract. The <a href={`${base}calculators/room-paint-calculator/`}>room paint calculator</a> turns a rectangular room into gallons. The <a href={`${base}calculators/date-difference-calculator/`}>day counter</a> still includes weekends: calendar year 2026 has 261 weekdays, 52 Saturdays, and 52 Sundays, and the elapsed count from 1 January to 31 December remains 364.</p><p>Pay calculators are split by the tax system they use. The <a href={`${base}calculators/texas-paycheck-calculator/`}>Texas paycheck calculator</a> and the <a href={`${base}calculators/florida-paycheck-calculator/`}>Florida paycheck calculator</a> estimate 2026 federal income tax, Social Security, and Medicare, with a state income tax line of zero. The <a href={`${base}calculators/california-paycheck-calculator/`}>California paycheck calculator</a> adds 2026 California income tax and State Disability Insurance. The <a href={`${base}calculators/washington-paycheck-calculator/`}>Washington paycheck calculator</a> keeps state income tax at $0 and subtracts 2026 Paid Leave and WA Cares. The <a href={`${base}calculators/scotland-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>Scotland take-home pay calculator</a> uses the 2026/27 Scottish income tax bands. The <a href={`${base}calculators/ontario-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>Ontario take-home pay calculator</a> uses 2026 federal and Ontario rates, CPP, and EI. The <a href={`${base}calculators/british-columbia-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>British Columbia take-home pay calculator</a> uses the 2026 B.C. brackets, including the 5.60% first rate and the tax reduction. The <a href={`${base}calculators/australia-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>Australia take-home pay calculator</a> uses the 2026–27 resident rates, the low income tax offset, and the Medicare levy. The <a href={`${base}calculators/england-stamp-duty-calculator/`}>England stamp duty calculator</a> applies residential SDLT, including first-time buyer relief and the additional-dwelling rates. Work tools also include an <a href={`${base}calculators/hourly-to-salary-calculator/`}>hourly to salary calculator</a>, a <a href={`${base}calculators/overtime-pay-calculator/`}>weekly overtime pay calculator</a>, and a <a href={`${base}calculators/401k-contribution-calculator/`}>2026 401(k) contribution calculator</a>. The <a href={`${base}calculators/rent-affordability-calculator/`}>rent affordability calculator</a> compares rent with 30% of gross income.</p><p>Another set of tools answers a narrower question than the page beside it. The <a href={`${base}calculators/illinois-paycheck-calculator/`}>2026 Illinois paycheck calculator</a> keeps the federal brackets and then applies the 4.95% Illinois rate after a $2,925 exemption, which is a different subtraction from the New York brackets or from a state line of zero. The <a href={`${base}calculators/manitoba-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>Manitoba take-home pay calculator</a> uses the 2026 Manitoba brackets, 10.8%, 12.75%, and 17.4%, with the $15,780 basic personal amount, on top of the same federal, CPP, and EI figures as Alberta. The <a href={`${base}calculators/victoria-stamp-duty-calculator/`}>Victoria stamp duty calculator</a> applies Victorian land transfer duty, including the first home buyer concession through $750,000 and the 8% foreign purchaser additional duty. The <a href={`${base}calculators/us-business-days-calculator/`}>US business days calculator</a> counts inclusive weekdays and can remove the 11 federal holidays. For 2026 that leaves 250 business days, against 261 weekdays and against the 364 elapsed days from 1 January to 31 December on the day counter. The <a href={`${base}calculators/mulch-calculator/`}>mulch calculator</a> turns a bed measured in feet, and a depth in inches, into cubic yards and 2 or 3 cubic foot bags. A 10 by 20 foot bed at 3 inches is 25 of the 2 cubic foot bags, which is not the bag count on the concrete page.</p><p>Five more tools fill gaps those pages leave. The <a href={`${base}calculators/pennsylvania-paycheck-calculator/`}>2026 Pennsylvania paycheck calculator</a> applies the 3.07% state tax to wages before a 401(k), then a local earned income tax rate you type and a flat local services tax. At $65,000, single, with a 1% local rate and $52, the two-week headline is $1,988.85. The <a href={`${base}calculators/saskatchewan-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>Saskatchewan take-home pay calculator</a> uses the 2026 brackets, 10.5%, 12.5%, and 14.5%, and a $20,381 basic personal amount. At $70,000 the monthly headline is $4,389.11, between Alberta and Manitoba on the same federal, CPP, and EI lines. The <a href={`${base}calculators/queensland-stamp-duty-calculator/`}>Queensland stamp duty calculator</a> follows the Queensland Revenue Office scales, including $6,555 of transfer duty on a $730,000 established first home. The <a href={`${base}calculators/uk-working-days-calculator/`}>UK working days calculator</a> counts inclusive weekdays and can remove bank holidays. England and Wales have 253 working days in 2026, against 250 US business days and against 261 weekdays. The <a href={`${base}calculators/gravel-calculator/`}>gravel calculator</a> turns the same 10 by 20 foot, 3 inch area the mulch page uses into 2.625 short tons of dry gravel at 105 lb per cubic foot.</p><p>Five further tools answer a different statute or a different unit. The <a href={`${base}calculators/ohio-paycheck-calculator/`}>2026 Ohio paycheck calculator</a> follows Ohio Revised Code 5747.02: no nonbusiness tax on the first $26,050 of Ohio taxable income, then $332 plus 2.75% of the excess, after a personal exemption. At $65,000, single, with one exemption and the school district and city rates left at zero, Ohio tax is $1,344.00 and the two-week headline is $2,040.90. The <a href={`${base}calculators/nova-scotia-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>Nova Scotia take-home pay calculator</a> uses the 2026 brackets, starting at 8.79%, and a $11,932 basic personal amount. At $70,000 the monthly headline is $4,208.02, which is $2,173.04 below Saskatchewan on the same federal, CPP, and EI lines. The <a href={`${base}calculators/scotland-lbtt-calculator/`}>Scotland LBTT calculator</a> applies residential Land and Buildings Transaction Tax, including first-time buyer relief of up to £600 and the 8% additional dwelling supplement. A £250,000 main home is £2,100, against £2,500 of SDLT on the England page. The <a href={`${base}calculators/canada-business-days-calculator/`}>Canada business days calculator</a> removes statutory holidays for Ontario, British Columbia, or Alberta. Ontario has 253 business days in 2026, British Columbia 250, and Alberta 252, against 261 weekdays. The <a href={`${base}calculators/5k-pace-calculator/`}>5K pace calculator</a> turns a finish time into minutes per kilometre and per mile. A 25:00 5K is 5:00 per kilometre and 8:02.8 per mile, which is not a calorie total.</p><p>Five further tools use a different statute or a different unit from the page beside them. The <a href={`${base}calculators/michigan-paycheck-calculator/`}>2026 Michigan paycheck calculator</a> applies 4.25% after a $5,900 exemption. At $65,000, single, with one exemption and no city tax, Michigan tax is $2,511.75 and the two-week headline is $1,995.99. Ohio on the same wages is $1,344.00 of state tax and $2,040.90 every two weeks. A Detroit resident on the Michigan wage adds $1,545.60 of city tax. The <a href={`${base}calculators/new-brunswick-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>New Brunswick take-home pay calculator</a> uses the 2026 brackets, 9.40%, 14%, 16%, and 19.5%, and a $13,664 basic personal amount. At $70,000 the monthly headline is $4,336.82, which is $128.80 above Nova Scotia on the same federal, CPP, and EI lines. The <a href={`${base}calculators/wales-land-transaction-tax-calculator/`}>Wales land transaction tax calculator</a> follows the GOV.WALES residential tables. A £280,000 main home is £3,300. A £250,000 main home is £1,500, against £2,500 of SDLT and £2,100 of LBTT. The <a href={`${base}calculators/floor-tile-calculator/`}>floor tile calculator</a> counts tiles from a grout joint. A 10 by 12 foot floor with 12 inch tiles, a 1/8 inch joint, and 10% waste is 130 tiles, 13 boxes of 10. The <a href={`${base}calculators/fuel-economy-converter/`}>fuel economy converter</a> separates the US gallon from the imperial gallon. 30 US mpg is 7.84 L/100 km and 36.03 UK mpg. The same digits read as UK mpg are 9.42 L/100 km.</p><p>Five further tools use a statute or a measurement the pages above do not. The <a href={`${base}calculators/georgia-paycheck-calculator/`}>2026 Georgia paycheck calculator</a> applies the 4.99% rate in HB 463 after a $15,000 single standard deduction. At $65,000, single, with no dependents, Georgia tax is $2,495.00 and the two-week headline is $1,996.63. The <a href={`${base}calculators/north-carolina-paycheck-calculator/`}>North Carolina paycheck calculator</a> uses the 3.99% rate for taxable years after 2025 and a $12,750 standard deduction. The same wage is $2,084.78 of North Carolina tax and $2,012.41 every two weeks. The <a href={`${base}calculators/quebec-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>Quebec take-home pay calculator</a> uses QPP, QPIP, the 1.30% Quebec EI rate, and the 16.5% federal abatement. At $70,000 the monthly headline is $4,253.73, which is $83.09 below New Brunswick because the payroll system is not the same. The <a href={`${base}calculators/western-australia-stamp-duty-calculator/`}>Western Australia stamp duty calculator</a> uses the first home owner rate for an agreement entered into on or after 7 May 2026. A $650,000 home is $8,075.00, against $24,890.00 on the general rate. The <a href={`${base}calculators/square-footage-calculator/`}>square footage calculator</a> turns 12 feet 6 inches by 10 feet into 125.00 square feet. The 10 by 12 floor on the tile page is 120.00 square feet here, and 132.00 square feet after 10% extra.</p><p>Five further tools answer a payment, a price, a state, a province, or a sheet count the pages above do not. The <a href={`${base}calculators/credit-card-payoff-calculator/`}>credit card payoff calculator</a> turns a $5,000 balance at 21.99% into 34 months when the fixed payment is $200, with $1,748.71 of interest. The same balance at $150 takes 52 months and $2,795.72 of interest. The <a href={`${base}calculators/house-affordability-calculator/`}>how much house calculator</a>, on $120,000 of gross income, $400 of other monthly debts, a $60,000 down payment, 6.5% for 30 years, $3,600 of tax, and $1,800 of insurance, solves a $431,795.43 home and a $371,795.43 loan. Principal and interest on that loan is $2,350.00, the same figure the mortgage page returns for that loan. The <a href={`${base}calculators/virginia-paycheck-calculator/`}>2026 Virginia paycheck calculator</a> charges $2,923.40 of Virginia tax on $65,000 single with one $930 exemption, and the two-week headline is $1,980.16. Georgia on that wage is $2,495.00 and $1,996.63. The <a href={`${base}calculators/prince-edward-island-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>Prince Edward Island take-home pay calculator</a> uses the 2026 brackets from 9.50% through 20% and a $15,000 basic personal amount. At $70,000 the monthly headline is $4,281.99, which is $54.83 below New Brunswick and $73.97 above Nova Scotia on the same federal, CPP, and EI lines. The <a href={`${base}calculators/drywall-calculator/`}>drywall calculator</a> counts sheets. A 12 by 10 foot room with 8 foot walls, 36 square feet of openings, the ceiling, and 10% waste needs 15 of the 4 by 8 sheets. The square footage page does not count those sheets.</p><p>Five further tools cover a conversion, a retail tax, a state, a province, and a conveyance the pages above do not. The <a href={`${base}calculators/celsius-to-fahrenheit-calculator/`}>Celsius to Fahrenheit calculator</a> uses °F = °C × 9/5 + 32. 180°C is 356°F, and a chart that prints 350°F is six degrees low. 72°F is 22.22°C on the headline and 22.2222°C before that rounding. The <a href={`${base}calculators/sales-tax-calculator/`}>sales tax calculator</a> adds a rate or removes it. $100 at 8.25% is $8.25 of tax and a $108.25 total. New Jersey’s statewide rate on 1 July 2026 is 6.625%, which is $3.31 on $49.99 and a $53.30 total. The <a href={`${base}calculators/new-jersey-paycheck-calculator/`}>2026 New Jersey paycheck calculator</a> uses Table A. At $65,000 single with one $1,000 exemption, New Jersey tax is $2,043.50 and the two-week headline is $2,014.00. Virginia on that wage is $2,923.40 and $1,980.16. A traditional 401(k) does not reduce the New Jersey tax. The <a href={`${base}calculators/newfoundland-and-labrador-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>Newfoundland and Labrador take-home pay calculator</a> uses the 2026 brackets from 8.7% and a $13,094 basic personal amount, not the July withholding catch-up of $15,000. At $70,000 the monthly headline is $4,308.58, which is $26.59 above Prince Edward Island on the same federal, CPP, and EI lines. The <a href={`${base}calculators/south-australia-stamp-duty-calculator/`}>South Australia stamp duty calculator</a> charges $26,830.00 on a $600,000 home. An eligible first buyer of a new home pays $0.00, with no price cap. A foreign person adds 7%, and the $600,000 headline becomes $68,830.00. Western Australia’s first home at $650,000 is $8,075.00, not this scale.</p><p>Five further tools answer a ratio, a height formula, a state, a territory, and a conveyance the pages above do not. The <a href={`${base}calculators/debt-to-income-ratio-calculator/`}>debt-to-income ratio calculator</a> keeps housing apart from other debts. On $8,000 of gross monthly income, a $2,200 housing payment and $400 of other debts is 27.50% front-end and 32.50% back-end. The how-much-house sample, $2,800 of housing on $10,000 a month plus $400 of other debts, is 28.00% and 32.00% here. The <a href={`${base}calculators/ideal-weight-calculator/`}>ideal weight calculator</a> uses Devine, Robinson, and Miller. A man at 175 cm has a Devine headline of 70.5 kg, which is 70.46 kg before rounding. The BMI page, given 70.5 kg and 175 cm, shows BMI 23. That ratio is not Devine. The <a href={`${base}calculators/arizona-paycheck-calculator/`}>2026 Arizona paycheck calculator</a> applies a flat 2.5% after a $15,750 standard deduction. At $65,000 single, Arizona tax is $1,231.25 and the two-week headline is $2,045.24. New Jersey on that wage is $2,043.50 and $2,014.00, and a 401(k) reduces Arizona tax only. The <a href={`${base}calculators/tasmania-stamp-duty-calculator/`}>Tasmania stamp duty calculator</a> charges $20,372.50 on a $550,000 home. An eligible first buyer of an established home pays $0.00 only if the transfer settles on or before 30 June 2026 and the value is at or under $750,000. A foreign person adds 8%, and the $550,000 headline becomes $64,372.50. South Australia’s general duty at $600,000 is $26,830.00, against $22,497.50 on this Tasmanian scale. The <a href={`${base}calculators/northwest-territories-take-home-pay-calculator/`}>Northwest Territories take-home pay calculator</a> uses the 2026 brackets from 5.9% to 14.05% and an $18,198 basic personal amount. At $70,000 the monthly headline is $4,537.04, which is $228.46 above Newfoundland and Labrador on the same federal, CPP, and EI lines, because territorial tax is $3,197.57 rather than $5,938.98.</p><p>Five further tools cover a due date, simple interest, two state paychecks, and a territory conveyance the pages above do not. The <a href={`${base}calculators/pregnancy-due-date-calculator/`}>pregnancy due date calculator</a> uses Naegele’s rule. A last menstrual period of 1 January 2026 and a 28-day cycle is due 8 October 2026, and gestational age on 1 April 2026 is 12 weeks and 6 days. A 35-day cycle moves the due date to 15 October 2026 and leaves that week count unchanged. The <a href={`${base}calculators/simple-interest-calculator/`}>simple interest calculator</a> multiplies principal, rate, and time. $10,000 at 5% for 3 years is $1,500.00 of interest and an $11,500.00 total. The compound interest page, with no monthly deposit, turns the same inputs into $11,614.72. The <a href={`${base}calculators/colorado-paycheck-calculator/`}>2026 Colorado paycheck calculator</a> applies a flat 4.40% to federal taxable income. At $65,000 single, Colorado tax is $2,151.60 and the two-week headline is $2,009.84. Arizona on that wage is $1,231.25 and $2,045.24. The <a href={`${base}calculators/massachusetts-paycheck-calculator/`}>2026 Massachusetts paycheck calculator</a> charges 5% after a $4,400 exemption. The same wage is $3,030.00 of state tax and $1,976.06 every two weeks. A 4% surtax applies only above $1,107,750 of taxable income. The <a href={`${base}calculators/act-stamp-duty-calculator/`}>ACT stamp duty calculator</a> uses the 2026–27 conveyance scales. An $800,000 owner-occupier pays $22,158.00, an investor pays $25,150.00, and an eligible home buyer with a contract on or after 1 July 2026 pays $0.00. Tasmania’s general duty at $550,000 is $20,372.50, on a different statute.</p></section>
</Layout>
